W", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 748910, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01SxCSvHxkqE9NiSjsGSTAkW", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 753394, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding per FIN-212. That's why `test_half_even` failed: 2.665 rounded up to 2.67 instead of down to 2.66.\n- **The fix:** I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on the branch `fix/money-round-half-even`. That's the only change.\n- **CI:** The first run passed, but the PR couldn't be opened because the branch was behind main. I merged the latest main into the branch, confirmed the fix was still there, and ran CI again. That run (ci-0002, commit 0a9452f727) also passed.\n- **PR:** #101 is at https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory system didn't recognise that ID, so I went by the test and the docstring. I haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NZ8bBruTrXyWuF9Vk8nNVo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_015WxCZrTKWwRpdaTLEXuynX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01U7DQYgZ2zashposcBSFjo3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_adv